WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.640
A-list actor, camping gear spokesman, makeup&nbsp;
artist – Jeremy Renner has worn many hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.584
throughout his life. These are some of the&nbsp;
weirder parts you may have forgotten about.

00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:12.060
A lot of celebrities launched apps in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:17.040
mid-2010s, and Jeremy Renner certainly wasn't the&nbsp;
only one who lacked Kardashian-level fame at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.300
time. So while the genesis of the Jeremy Renner&nbsp;
app certainly makes the actor appear a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.120
eccentric, it might not have seemed like a totally&nbsp;
insane idea in 2017. Today, the Jeremy Renner app&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.440
absolutely seems like a totally insane idea, but&nbsp;
that's only because of our power of hindsight.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.480
Sadly, the Jeremy Renner App devolved into a&nbsp;
clustermuck of mythic proportions. Folks didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.280
always comprehend what it was supposed to do or&nbsp;
why it should cost money. Its service was prone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.440
glitches and confusing info. Trolls impersonating&nbsp;
Renner and potentially-upsetting figures like OJ&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.088
Simpson and Casey Anthony inundated the service.&nbsp;
In 2019, Renner himself pulled the plug.

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:55.800
While we obviously don't have any&nbsp;
knowledge of the man's personal finances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.120
it's possible Jeremy Renner doesn't need to&nbsp;
continue acting. Even if Marvel decided to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:04.320
kill off Clint Barton, it's not like he'd be&nbsp;
wanting for roles or – presumably – money.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.220
Ever since his acting career began&nbsp;
generating cash in the early '00s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.440
Renner's cultivated a side business in buying,&nbsp;
renovating, and re-selling multi-million dollar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.901
residences. As of a 2016 Bloomberg report, Renner&nbsp;
had purchased and remodeled upwards of 20 houses.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.280
"So you and your buddy buy the house,&nbsp;
move into it, while you're renovating?"

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.480
"And then start tearing it apart."

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.100
In an interview with Bloomberg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.180
Renner had this to say about his relatively&nbsp;
unglamorous moonlighting in real estate:

00:01:38.825 --> 00:01:39.840
Before Renner caught a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.760
break with S.W.A.T. in 2003, he performed around&nbsp;
Hollywood in a rock group called Sons of Ben,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.240
which included members of Tonic. You&nbsp;
might not immediately recognize the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.020
name "Tonic," but you've probably heard the&nbsp;
group's 1996's alternative rock hit "If You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.503
Could Only See." Renner told&nbsp;
Playboy in a 2015 interview:

00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:02.820
Like a handful of other celebrities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.540
Jeremy Renner has an Amazon store.&nbsp;
This store contains fishing gear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.080
a portable cooler, plenty of archery&nbsp;
paraphernalia, poison ivy ointment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.800
a flannel shirt, and jeans — all the&nbsp;
products necessary for Jeremy Renner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.180
or an individual hoping to emulate Jeremy Renner,&nbsp;
to go on an adventure in the great outdoors.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.800
However, an investigation from Slate&nbsp;
raises questions. While not making any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.820
assertions about Renner's actual acumen as an&nbsp;
outdoorsman, the article does point out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.420
Renner doesn't look like he knows what he's&nbsp;
doing while posing with camping gear for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.260
Amazon promotional shots. Renner points&nbsp;
his bow and arrow away from its target,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.220
and he sits next to a campfire that's&nbsp;
surrounded by flammable objects — both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.660
obvious safety hazards. Additionally, he holds&nbsp;
binoculars without looking through the lenses.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.800
In fairness, Renner doesn't hunt or fish,&nbsp;
which explains why his photo with a reel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.760
and rod combo looks a little awkward.&nbsp;
He's also modeling these products, so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.159
you know – it wouldn't make sense to hide&nbsp;
the celebrity face behind those binoculars.

00:02:55.159 --> 00:02:56.460
Let's face it — human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.760
civilization is insecure about&nbsp;
its masculinity. On that note,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.600
Jeremy Renner's a guy who plays tough dudes&nbsp;
in movies. It just so happens that he once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:09.240
worked as a makeup artist at a Lancôme outlet in&nbsp;
a Modesto, California, mall. And numerous Renner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.440
profiles have treated this fact as much more&nbsp;
interesting and unusual than it actually is.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.000
According to the first episode of "The Renner&nbsp;
Files" podcast, his stint with Lancôme took place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.040
in the '90s. Back then, the eventual cast member&nbsp;
of Avengers: Endgame needed a day job to cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.060
basic living essentials between commercial gigs&nbsp;
and stage plays. Renner explained on the podcast:

00:03:36.186 --> 00:03:37.980
Nowadays, Jeremy Renner is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.000
guy you call when your movie needs a Han&nbsp;
Solo-type of dude — irreverent and rough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.040
around the edges but basically well-intentioned.&nbsp;
Earlier in his career, Hollywood nudged Renner in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.420
a very different direction. At that point,&nbsp;
agents and casting directors saw him more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.040
in the frequently villainous mold of Jared&nbsp;
Leto than as a potential next Harrison Ford.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.840
And here's a little-known fact: The Avengers was&nbsp;
actually Renner's second collaboration with Buffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.620
the Vampire Slayer creator and Avengers&nbsp;
director Joss Whedon. As it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.400
Renner played Penn — a vampire and&nbsp;
serial killer who terrorizes Los&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.840
Angeles — in a 2000 episode of the&nbsp;
Buffy spinoff Angel. And in 2002,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.120
Renner added his first headlining movie role to&nbsp;
his resume with the true crime biopic Dahmer.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.380
If S.W.A.T. hadn't come along and shifted his&nbsp;
career trajectory, Renner might've evolved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:26.365
into the sort of actor whose name pops up&nbsp;
whenever it's time to cast another Joker.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.860
It's routinely reported that Jeremy Renner does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.480
his own stunts whenever humanly possible, and he's&nbsp;
also never been shy about telling interviewers his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:38.460
attitude about fear. He has what you might call&nbsp;
mixed feelings about fear. He's never said he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:44.517
hates it, but he clearly considers it a somewhat&nbsp;
overrated instinct. Renner told Playboy in 2015:

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.960
By the magazine's account, Renner claims he did&nbsp;
something scary every day from his early 20s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.120
into his early 30s, and the result is a reduced&nbsp;
vulnerability to fear. Renner told the magazine:

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:12.480
"You're a wild man, you know that? He's a wild&nbsp;
man, you know that? I want to shake your hand."

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.420
As he has no idea if it's&nbsp;
ever helped him on auditions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.860
Renner doesn't credit his supposed ability to&nbsp;
neutralize fear for his acting success. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.100
he does say limited vulnerability&nbsp;
to fear made him a better actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.199
in the respect that it allows him to deliver the&nbsp;
most honest possible version of his characters.

00:05:28.199 --> 00:05:29.340
To be clear, we think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.360
it's unlikely that Jeremy Renner will ever&nbsp;
convince himself that he truly is Clint Barton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.080
and get picked up by law enforcement after a&nbsp;
period of wandering around the Nevada desert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:41.220
shooting arrows at HYDRA agents only he&nbsp;
can see. But if it ever comes to that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.780
at least he's got the outfit handy. During&nbsp;
a 2021 Jimmy Kimmel appearance, Renner said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.580
he never left any Marvel movie set with props as&nbsp;
souvenirs, having been instructed not to do that.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.420
Later, he found out the rest of the Avengers&nbsp;
main cast just took whatever they felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.860
like whenever they wanted. In fact, Chris&nbsp;
Hemsworth owns multiple Mjölnirs and keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.460
the ill-gotten magic hammers scattered&nbsp;
around his house. After learning this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.900
Renner helped himself to a Hawkeye costume.&nbsp;
Today, when Jeremy Renner volunteers at his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.500
daughter's elementary school, he&nbsp;
does so in full-on Hawkeye regalia.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.920
"So I said fine if I'm going to do it,&nbsp;
I'm going to do it dressed as Hawkeye."

00:06:18.713 --> 00:06:20.940
As is widely reported, Jeremy Renner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:25.680
prefers to do his own stunts. As you can imagine,&nbsp;
that makes injuries on set more likely. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:31.140
to Vanity Fair, a scene for the 2018 movie Tag&nbsp;
took a disastrous turn that subjected Renner to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:37.080
a 20-foot fall and a pile of broken bones. Renner&nbsp;
broke both his arms, didn't notice, and agreed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.689
do another take of the same stunt before heading&nbsp;
over to the hospital. The actor told Vanity Fair:

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.420
In this instance, continuing on meant the&nbsp;
special effects department had to go the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:56.760
extra mile and provide Renner with CG limbs to&nbsp;
fill in for his temporarily immobilized arms.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.095
"It was the only time I ever&nbsp;
got injured was on this comedy."

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.720
Unlike the many other celebrity cameos&nbsp;
sprinkled throughout Glass Onion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.320
A Knives Out Mystery, Jeremy Renner's&nbsp;
appearance matters to the plot and doesn't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.920
in the strictest sense, actually&nbsp;
happen. At least not in the flesh.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:15.240
Among fan-favorite cameos like Hugh&nbsp;
Grant as Benoit Blanc's husband Phillip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.960
Serena Williams actually on a live&nbsp;
monitor in the home gym waiting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.740
someone to ask for a workout, and all of&nbsp;
Blanc's Zoom-linked Among Us playmates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.580
Jeremy Renner's face only appears on the&nbsp;
label of his own fictional hot sauce.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.540
"That's Jeremy Renner's small batch hot sauce. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.340
let him invest. He sends me&nbsp;
like a pallet every year."

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:38.400
In a joke so meta as to be utterly believable,&nbsp;
Renner's penchant for side hustles -– celebrity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.840
app, Amazon store, house flipping, "rock music"&nbsp;
-– was poked fun at with the introduction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.800
a private label hot sauce by the actor&nbsp;
that shows up at a pivotal point in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.120
story to provide a crucial function. Is&nbsp;
writer-director Rian Johnson an actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:56.586
genius or is he just a huge "Hot Ones" fan?&nbsp;
What if he's both? The world may never know.

00:07:56.586 --> 00:08:01.620
Announced in February 2022 at the Television&nbsp;
Critics' Association Press Tour, Rennervations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:07.560
is a four-episode reality TV documentary&nbsp;
that will stream on Disney+ in 2023. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:11.760
announcement outlines that the show finds Renner&nbsp;
traveling the world and helping communities by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.680
"reimagining unique purpose-built vehicles."&nbsp;
We're not exactly sure what that means, but in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:21.840
December 2022 Renner shared a short clip to his&nbsp;
Instagram promoting the upcoming show by saying,

00:08:25.729 --> 00:08:30.360
Given Renner's established history of remodeling&nbsp;
homes -– not to mention the play on words of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.380
show's title -– it seems fair to assume that the&nbsp;
actor and his team will be renovating something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:39.120
for families or communities in need. This&nbsp;
could mean RVs, school buses, food trucks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.260
mobile health clinics, or roving libraries.&nbsp;
Depending on the situation, those types of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.640
vehicles revamped could make a huge difference&nbsp;
in people's lives. And with only four episodes on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:52.740
the docket, audiences might enjoy a little slice&nbsp;
of feel-good TV amidst the chaos of daily life.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:09:00.000
As 2022 ended, Jeremy Renner's Nevada home was&nbsp;
snowed in. On January 1, 2023, Renner was plowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.100
the roads nearby with his Snowcat when there was&nbsp;
an accident and Renner suffered critical injuries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:10.080
to his legs and chest. The actor was airlifted&nbsp;
to a local hospital and underwent two surgeries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:14.880
for blunt chest trauma and orthopedic injuries.&nbsp;
Following the surgeries, Renner was moved into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.740
ICU and listed in "critical but stable condition,"&nbsp;
according to a statement released by his family.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:24.120
Celebrity news outlet Extra reported on&nbsp;
January 2nd that Renner was "conscious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:28.920
stable, and speaking" prior to his surgeries.&nbsp;
On January 3rd, Renner shared a new photo to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.360
his Instagram, revealing some of his injuries.&nbsp;
CNN reported further details of the incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.380
clarifying that the Snowcat started rolling&nbsp;
away when Renner was not in the driver's seat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:41.520
and that the accident occurred as he attempted&nbsp;
to get back in. The Washoe County Sheriff's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.880
Department has impounded the vehicle and&nbsp;
will inspect it for mechanical issues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.080
but called the event "a tragic accident"&nbsp;
and does not suspect foul play of any kind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:53.880
Samantha Mast, Renner's publicist, released&nbsp;
a statement earlier that same day that said,

